       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. 20 mg is double the FDA-labeled maximum for amlodipine, which is 10 mg once daily. Doses above 10 mg raise the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia. They usually add little extra blood pressure control.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter 10 mg PO daily.** This is the standard maximum dose.\n- **Keep amlodipine at 10 mg and add a second agent.** An ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide-type diuretic would be typical.\n- **Enter 20 mg anyway.** I can do this if the dose is intentional, for example because of a specific clinical reason. Please confirm, and tell me if you want a note on the order documenting the rationale.\n\nWhich would you like?"
